Please look into observeEvents these will help you greatly with situations like this. Here is a solution that fits what you are looking for.

library(shiny)
library(ggplot2)
shinyApp(
  ui = fluidPage(
    textInput("textT", label = h5("Title"), value = ""),
    textInput("textX", label = h5("X Axis Label"), value = ""),
    actionButton("Btn", "", "push me"),
    plotOutput('plot1')),
  server = function(input, output) {

   observe({
      input$textT
      input$textX
      output$plot1 = renderPlot({})
    })
   observeEvent(input$Btn, {
     output$plot1 = renderPlot({
        ggplot(mtcars, aes(x= gear, y= carb)) + geom_line() +ggtitle(input$textT) + xlab(input$textX)
      })
   })

})

Although I am unsure if the first observer event is proper coding style, it does work. Depending on your program you should be able to do something along these lines in a better manner.

Hope this helps,

Amber James

