I've sent you a pull request on your GitHub repo.

1) Did away with the renderUI, replaced with updateSelectInput.
2) Don't wait for the first column to be populated to make choices available in the second. I thought about this and the interaction model feels a lot better to me this way.
3) Extract out common logic into functions.

However another way to do this would be to simply use a DT data table <http://rstudio.github.io/DT/>, which can include filter boxes over each column: http://rstudio.github.io/DT/#column-filters

