In all likelihood, a database running on your laptop is not accessible from the shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io> servers. If you are running on a corporate or campus network, you should contact your network administrator and discuss with them how to get this setup properly. In short your laptop running the database will need a public IP address and firewall rules to allow the shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io> servers to connect to it.

Your other option would be to host your database using a 3rd party service such as Amazon RDS which can be configured to allow connections from shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io> servers.

Hope that helps
-Andy

