Anthony,

As I said on the other thread you posted: what needs to happen here is that the shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io> servers need to be able to connect to YOUR mysql servers. This is not something that shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io> controls, but rather is something your local network must be setup to allow. Typically this done with firewall rules or NATs, but that's entirely dependent on your local network. If you are on a corporate or campus network, you should reach out to your network administrator.

-Andy

