Don't forget that ui.R code is still R code. I'd follow the same formatting guidelines and use the same formatting tools. And also, an oft-overlooked technique for ui.R is to write functions for common idioms--the same as for regular R code.

On Fri, Jul 17, 2015 at 10:53 AM Robert Lehr <robert...@gmail.com> wrote:

> Sometimes I use the # to help visually separate blocks of ui.R script.
>
> block 1
> #-------------------------------------------------
> block 2
> #-------------------------------------------------
> block 3
> #-------------------------------------------------
> block 4
>
>
> I also add # end of function_name at the ends of long functions. Look below for example.
> Aside from that, keep your indentation style consistent
>
> EX: (I don't really need #---------------------- in this one, but they can be useful in longer or more convoluted ui.R.
> shinyUI(
>   fluidPage(
>      titlePanel(),
>
>      sidebarLayout(
>         sidebarPanel(
>            textInput(),
>            textInput(),
>            textInput(),
>            actionButton(),
>            uiOutput("chooseDatabases")
>                     ), #sidebarPanel() end parantheses
>
>         mainPanel(
>            tabsetPanel(
>                   tabPanel("",
>                            plotOutput("graph1", width = 1200, height = 700)
>                            ),
>                   tabPanel("",
>                            plotOutput("graph2", width = 1200, height = 700)
>                   ),
>                   tabPanel("",
>                            plotOutput("graph3", width = 1200, height = 700)
>                   ),
>                   tabPanel("",
>                            plotOutput("graph4", width = 1200, height = 700)
>                   ),
>                   tabPanel("",
>                            plotOutput("graph5", width = 1200, height = 700)
>                   ),
>                   tabPanel("",
>                            verbatimTextOutput(""),
>                            verbatimTextOutput(""),
>                            verbatimTextOutput("")
>                           ),
>                   tabPanel("Table",
>                            tableOutput("Table1"),
>                            tableOutput("Table2"),
>                            tableOutput("Table3"),
>                            tableOutput("Table4"),
>                            tableOutput("Table5")
>                            )
>                        )#tabsetPanel() end parantheses
>                 )#mainPanel() end parantheses
>             )#sidebarLayout() end parantheses
>        )#fluidPage() end parantheses
>    )#shinyUI() end parantheses
>
>
> On Friday, July 17, 2015 at 12:25:56 PM UTC-5, Iain Wallace wrote:
