Hi Bastien !!

Sorry for the delay !

I tried to isolate flag$temp only in the observe and as it did not work, I gave up !!
But yes when I isolate it in the renderUI output$choix, it works !!!

Thank you very very much Bastien.

I had another solution, less elegant:

library("shiny")
runApp(list(
  ui = bootstrapPage(
    uiOutput("choix"),
    uiOutput("valid")
  ),

  server = function(input, output,session) {

    #
    flag = reactiveValues(temp = list(

      sample1 = list(

        type = NA,
        temoin = c(0,0,0,0,0),
        names = c("ech1", "ech2"),
        dataInterm = NA,
        dataFinal = NA
      ),

      sample2 = list(

        type = NA,
        temoin = c(0,0,0,0,0),
        dataFinal = NA,
        dataInterm = NA,
        names = c("ech3", "ech4")
      )

    ))

    output$choix <- renderUI({

      selectInput("exchoix","",choices = names(flag$temp))

    })

    output$valid <- renderUI({

      actionButton("valid","valider")

    })

    observe({
      if(is.null(input$valid)){}
      else{
        isolate({
          if(input$valid > 0){
            flag$temp[[grep(isolate(input$exchoix),names(flag$temp))]]$temoin[1] = 1

            updateSelectInput(session, "exchoix", selected = input$exchoix)
            print(isolate(flag$temp)[[grep(isolate(input$exchoix),names(flag$temp))]]$temoin)
          }
        })
      }

    })

  }

))

Again thank you very much!!

Cheers,

cha

